{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"An ETF seeking relief beyond Rule 6c-11 generally files an exemptive application with the SEC under the relevant Investment Company Act provisions. Staff reviews it and may request changes or additional information. If the application is ready to proceed, the Commission issues a **notice** and publishes it; the notice invites interested persons to request a hearing by the stated deadline. Notice is not approval. After the notice period, absent a hearing request or other impediment, the Commission may issue an **order** granting the requested relief.\n\n**Expedited review under Rule 0-5(d)** is available when the application is substantially identical to a recent application the Commission has previously granted and raises no novel issues. The 45-day clock is the staff’s target for issuing the **notice** after filing—not a deadline for granting the order or a promise of approval. It therefore does not establish a universal total approval time."}}
